<title>USA: Equifax announces Asian initiatives.</title>
<headline>Equifax announces Asian initiatives.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Equifax Inc announced several new Asian initiatives on Monday, including a regionwide marketing alliance with International Business Machines Corp.</p>
<p>The deal with IBM provides for computer, management and software solutions to support credit and debit cards throughout Asia and the Pacific Rim.</p>
<p>The company also said it has been selected by Thailand's finance and banking industries as their technology partner to establish the nation's first automated credit bureau.  </p>
<p>In India, Equifax has formed a joint venture with Venture Infotek to create the first ever third-party credit card processor in that country.</p>
<p>The company also announced major sales of card-processing software to the International Bank of Asia in Hong Kong and to Takinfo Bank of Hungary.</p>
<p>In addition, Equifax said it was starting up its consumer credit information business in Mexico.</p>
</text>
